interfaces:
Rust, mp-contracts (new, pure, no I/O): pub enum DurableStore { Fold, Consume, Continue, Park } with fn feature(self) returning agent_run for Fold and Park and approval_continuation for Consume and Continue. pub fn refuse_unless_persistent(store: DurableStore, resolution: &Resolution<'_>) returns Result<(), Refusal>: Persistent is Ok; Refuse returns the resolver's own refusal unchanged; Zdr and Waived return Refusal::feature_not_supported(store.feature()). pub fn refuse_unless_persistent_class(store: DurableStore, retention_class: &str) returns Result<(), Refusal>, Ok only for the string persistent (the runs.retention_class value; the golden vocabulary maps zdr, persistent and waived to zdr, persistent and zdr_waived). pub const fn continuation_mode_for(persistent: bool, enabled: bool) returns loop only when both are true, otherwise the empty string. pub fn build_continue_resume(approval_id: &str, claim_token: &str) returns an AgentResume with mode segment, empty brief and segment_no 0, meaning the executor owns numbering. pub fn validate_continue_resume(resume: &AgentResume) returns Result<(), &'static str>: resume_incomplete for a mode outside segment or loop, or an empty approval_id or claim_token; resume_segment_client_supplied when segment_no is not 0. The executor's enforce_resume and the gateway builder both call these.

Gateway (model-gateway, sse.rs): continue_preflight(enabled, run_status, approval_matches_run, approval_granted, continuation_mode, approval_consumed, persistent) adds continuation_already_consumed (409) when approval_consumed is true, and not_resumable (409) when persistent is false. persistent comes from crate::zdr_posture::decide_for(claims, &Route::plain(false)) matching TurnPosture::Persistent. continue_run keeps its ZDR gate and owner check. Approval consumed_at is already populated by GetApproval (session-core orchestration_grpc.rs 1230), so no proto change is needed for F6.

Session-core (SQL, consume): the approvals row joined to runs on run_id; the predicate is runs.retention_class = 'persistent' AND approvals.continuation_mode <> '' AND consumed_at IS NULL, and the refusal is feature approval_continuation.

Temporary trigger for stage s5 (created inside one transaction, dropped in cleanup; every object name is prefixed ws03_proof_):
CREATE TABLE ws03_proof_finalize_delay (tool TEXT PRIMARY KEY, seconds INT NOT NULL CHECK (seconds BETWEEN 1 AND 30), until TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL);
CREATE FUNCTION ws03_proof_finalize_delay_fn() RETURNS trigger LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$ DECLARE d INT; BEGIN SELECT seconds INTO d FROM ws03_proof_finalize_delay WHERE tool = NEW.tool AND until > now(); IF d IS NOT NULL AND OLD.status = 'reserved' AND NEW.status IN ('completed','failed') THEN PERFORM pg_sleep(d); END IF; RETURN NEW; END $$;
CREATE TRIGGER ws03_proof_finalize_delay BEFORE UPDATE ON session_tool_audit_intents FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION ws03_proof_finalize_delay_fn();
Cleanup: DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS ws03_proof_finalize_delay ON session_tool_audit_intents; DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS ws03_proof_finalize_delay_fn(); DROP TABLE IF EXISTS ws03_proof_finalize_delay;
Final check: SELECT count(*) FROM pg_trigger WHERE tgname LIKE 'ws03_proof%' AND NOT tgisinternal must return 0.

